## Summary

Fixes the stile issue a-thoren found while testing #366: "you can jump over the stile from too far away and the code assumes you're right next to it, meaning you don't always end up in the sheep pen". The cause is the shared `StileScript` (every `fullstyle` stile, including the Sheep Shearer pen's), so this is its own change rather than part of #366.

`StileScript.climbStile` climbed from wherever the interaction ended, toward the stile's far footprint tile. From a diagonal tile or from beside the stile along the fence the forced move started off line, and from the far side it moved the player one tile without crossing. The stile's two footprint tiles block walking (loc 12982: 1x2, blocks walk), so the player can't simply walk onto them either.

It now does what the official game does in an RSProx recording of the pen stile (1718, ticks 2328-2333):
1. The player walks to the tile just outside the footprint on their side, in line with the crossing (the side is chosen by coordinate across the fence). If they can't get there, nothing happens.
2. The tick after reaching that tile, a one-tile forced move onto the near footprint tile.
3. The next tick, the existing climb (`human_walk_style`, exactmove 30/94 cycles, facing the crossing) to the far footprint tile.
4. Three ticks later a one-tile forced move onto the tile beyond it.

The forced moves and the climb's exactmove use `TeleportType.Exempt`: crossing a fence isn't a teleport, and a teleport restriction must not leave the player standing on the stile. `climbOver` is shared with `FenceCrossingScript` (Gertrude's fence), which gets the same exemption.

